st Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning for this pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Integrated B.Ed with Educational Technology","Teaching Practicum","Educational Content Internship","Instructional Design + Multimedia Skills","LMS + Assessment","Digital Content Developer","Senior Content Developer / Instructional Designer","Learning Design Lead","Head of Content / Learning Experience Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal graduate profile"},{"type":"p","text":"An education professional who can combine pedagogy, instructional design, multimedia production, LMS technology, assessment, learning analytics and responsible AI to create engaging, accessible and measurable digital learning experiences."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment note","text":"Digital Content Developer is generally an education/EdTech content role rather than a regulated profession. The exact title and requirements vary by employer. For stronger employability, the student should graduate with a demonstrable digital-learning portfolio, not just an education degree and certifications."}]}]}